                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "As VR experiences go, this is a decent one given the price. The temple is interesting, if a bit basic, graphically, and the controls are standard real movement + teleport (my preferred method). However, I was unable to complete the game due to a warning that should be present on all VR games in the future with a particular feature, which is:\n\nCONTAINS SPIDERS\n\nSeriously, if you are an arachnophobe, it might be best skipping this. I played through A Chair In the Room and loved but, it giant spiders make me nope out of VR immediately. Could not complete for that reason, and likely won't play it again.\n\nSo, so long as you don't mind big ass spiders, give it a whirl.",
